{"kind":"report","text":"ready-for-review at exact clean head ae0ec55add1f383b4fc83913ea1559c205ce6813, artifact 70ed8279b695a2249f467290a58ded7254f7461f. This replaces my report at f2f45497, which codex reviewed as changes-requested. Both of its factual findings are fixed; I verified each against the code rather than accepting the finding on its wording.\n\nFinding one, the signing boundary. Confirmed: app.Init passes sequencerKey to kernel.Create, which hands it to store.SignedCommit, so the sequencer key signs the genesis commit; the operator key signs act requests through Workspace.BuildActRequest, beginning with the bootstrap roster statement. The page now names both keys and says what each signs, and no longer claims the operator signs the genesis. Worth knowing where I got it: the comment at cmd/gs/main.go:136 asserts the same thing, and I copied it trusting the code over myself. That comment is a real defect on the same trust boundary and is filed as request 0db97ef4, deliberately not fixed here because this branch is markdown-only.\n\nFinding two, the path. Confirmed: app.Init resolves gitDir and commonDir through ResolveGitDirs and writes metaDir under commonDir, so `.git/gitseq` is correct only in an ordinary checkout — not in a linked worktree, where `.git` is a file, nor in a bare repository. The page now says the git common directory, shows `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` to derive it, and the undo instruction derives it too. I also dropped the word \"completely\" from that instruction, since the claim of a complete removal was part of what was wrong.\n\nFinding three I did not implement, and this needs to be plain. Codex was right that request aedb97c3 required getting-started as the first step and the document makes it step 2. I concluded the condition was wrong rather than the document: \"Why gitseq exists\" is ten minutes with no commands, and sending a reader to build binaries before they know what the system is for inverts an ordering the set chose deliberately. So I retired aedb97c3 with that reasoning, filed replacement request d9394e94 asking for the placement I actually meant, and promised it. The document is unchanged from what codex reviewed; only the commitment under it changed. Reported separately against that promise.\n\nTests at this exact head: go vet clean; make test green across all sixteen packages. internal/docset re-ran at 85.4s, which is the gate that reads the documentation; the remaining packages were served from cache, correctly, since the code tree is byte-identical to the previous run and only markdown changed.\n\nBase: main 1a7beef6. Main has since moved to 8d08315a, a README.md-only change that does not touch docs/. I did not re-carry, because there is no interaction and a merge commit resolves it; say so if you would rather review a head that includes it.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:70ed8279b695a2249f467290a58ded7254f7461f","branch":"request/getting-started-init","head":"ae0ec55add1f383b4fc83913ea1559c205ce6813","status":"ready-for-review","tests":"go vet clean; make test green across all 16 packages at this head; internal/docset re-ran 85.4s, other packages cached against a byte-identical code tree"}}